To run site locally use:
bundle exec jekyll serve
To automatically reload webpage when changes are made
bundle exec jekyll serve --livereload 

don't forget to activate conda base. necessary for jupyter notebooks

if LoadError / "cannot load such file ... bundler-X.Y.Z":
1. which ruby   -> should be ~/.rbenv/shims/ruby. If it's /opt/homebrew/...,
   rbenv isn't loaded: source ~/.zshrc
2. gem install bundler -v X.Y.Z   (X.Y.Z = the BUNDLED WITH version at the
   bottom of Gemfile.lock)
3. bundle install

To standardize formatting:

npx prettier . --check

and then

npx prettier . --write

Ruby is now managed by rbenv, not brew. .ruby-version pins this folder to 4.0.7 (lives in ~/.rbenv/versions/). brew upgrade can't break it.

The Homebrew ruby is still installed but not in PATH anymore.
Gemfile.lock ends with BUNDLED WITH 4.0.20 (the bundler that ships with Ruby 4.0).

GitHub builds with ruby-version "4.0" in .github/workflows/deploy.yml.

To upgrade Ruby (about once a year):
rbenv install X.Y.Z
rbenv local X.Y.Z
gem install bundler -v <BUNDLED WITH version>   # or edit BUNDLED WITH to match bundle -v
bundle install
change ruby-version in deploy.yml to "X.Y" (series only; runner needs latest patch)
commit Gemfile.lock + deploy.yml, push, check Deploy site run

